{
  "dom_id": "step-q112141",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The growth of a mice colony is given by the formula $M(t)=6\\cdot {2}^{t},$ where $t$ is the time, in months, since the beginning of the observation. How many mice will the colony have after $5$ months?",
  "worked_solution": "To get the number of mice in the colony after $5$ months, we evaluate the function at $t=5.$ Substituting $t=5$ into the function $M(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M(5) & =6\\cdot {2}^{5} \\\\  & =6\\cdot 32 \\\\  & =192.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, after $5$ months there will be $192$ mice in the colony.",
